SUMMARY:Matthew Grasso’s 19th Annual Celebration of the 7-String Guitar
DESCRIPTION:The 19th Annual Celebration of the 7-String Guitar concert will showcase music consisting of both composed and improvised music for multi-stringed guitars. Dr. George England\, the guitar professor at Sacramento State University\, will perform on a period instrument\, the 14-stringed archlute. Matthew Grasso will perform original works for the extended 7-string by regional composers\, Sean O’Connor and Miyan Grasso\, as well as his own compositions. Trio Seven reunites to perform original transcriptions of movie and video game themes. \nThis annual concert on July 7th celebrates innovative guitar designs and a diversity of literature that highlights the artistry of the multistring guitar players. \nMusicians:\nMatthew Grasso – extended 7-string guitar\nEric Rasmussen – extended 7-string guitar\nSam Ritchie – extended 7-string guitar\nGeorge England – 14-stringed archlute \nWhen: Tuesday\, July 7th\, 2026\nTime: 7:07 pm\nLocation: Odd Fellows Hall (upper hall)\n415 2nd St\, Davis\, 95616\nDonation: $14 – $28
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/matthew-grassos-19th-annual-celebration-of-the-7-string-guitar/
LOCATION:Davis Odd Fellows
CATEGORIES:Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/7-7-2026_19th_Celebration_COLOR-scaled.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Matthew Grasso":MAILTO:mysticalgrasso@gmail.com
END:VEVENT
